cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mcmckit: minimal, plug-and-play MCMC samplers for Python"
abstract: >-
  mcmckit provides a compact, dependency-light set of MCMC samplers for Bayesian
  model updating and inverse problems in engineering, with an emphasis on
  structural dynamics and structural health monitoring. Each sampler is exposed
  as a single-step function with all state passed in and returned explicitly, so
  the sampling loop stays under the user's control and drops into existing code;
  full-run helpers wrapping the same functions are provided for when it does not
  need to. It includes random-walk Metropolis-Hastings, MALA and adaptive MALA,
  RAM, DRAM, Metropolis-within-Gibbs and Transitional MCMC (TMCMC) with
  log-evidence estimation, together with utilities for noise estimation,
  hierarchical models, sequential updating, model comparison and convergence
  diagnostics.
